    "body": "## Overview\n\nNemotron VL (`nano_nemotron_vl.py`, e.g. Nemotron 3.5 Super VL / Nemotron 3 Nano Omni) rejects a valid video request with HTTP 500 whenever the `<video>` placeholder directly follows non-whitespace text. This PR makes the model's multimodal processor re-encode text segments separately in the prompt-update fallback, as `minicpmv.py` already does for the same reason.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes `Expected there to be 1 prompt placeholders corresponding to 1 video items, but instead found 0 prompt placeholders!` for prompts such as `\"Describe this clip.<video>\"` (text part followed by a video part with no separator, or a user-supplied placeholder inside the text).\n- No behaviour change for prompts whose placeholder is already delimited (`\"...\\n<video>\"`): they still take the token-level path.\n- Model-local change only (one method override on `NanoNemotronVLMultiModalProcessor`, +56 lines); no change to the shared processor.\n\n## Validation\n\nRoot cause reproduced with the real Nemotron 3.5 Super VL tokenizer (`<video>` is not a vocabulary token):\n\n| prompt | token-level match | text fallback, joined re-encode | text fallback, segments encoded separately |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Describe this clip.<video>` | no (`.<`, `video`, `>`) | replacement not found (`.Frame` merge) | found |\n| `<video>\\nDescribe this clip.` | no (`>\\n`) | found | found |\n| `Describe this clip.\\n<video>` | yes | n/a | n/a |\n\nNew GPU-free tests in `tests/models/multimodal/test_nano_nemotron_vl.py` use a small tokenizer that reproduces both merges:\n\n- `test_video_placeholder_adjacent_to_text_is_replaced` (3 prompts): **fails without the fix** on the two adjacent prompts (`2 failed, 2 passed`) and passes with it (`4 passed`), run against an installed vLLM v0.32.0.\n- `test_video_placeholder_adjacent_to_text_needs_segment_encoding`: documents that `BaseMultiModalProcessor._apply_prompt_updates` alone loses the placeholder for this model.\n- Existing `test_nano_nemotron_vl.py`: `17 passed`.\n\n`ruff format` / `ruff check` clean on both files.\n\n## Details\n\nThe video `PromptReplacement` target is `cached_encode(tokenizer, \"<video>\")`, which yields `<`, `video`, `>` because `<video>` is not in the vocabulary (unlike `<image>`, `<img>`, `</img>`, which are added tokens). When text precedes the placeholder, BPE merges across the boundary (`.<`) and `apply_token_matches` finds nothing. The base class then falls back to `_apply_prompt_updates_via_text`, which joins `prompt_prefix + decoded_replacement + suffix` and re-encodes it in one pass; the video replacement begins with ordinary text (`Frame 1 sampled at 0.00 seconds: `), so the same kind of merge now happens at the new boundary (`.Frame`) and `find_mm_placeholders` cannot locate the replacement sequence.\n\n`_apply_prompt_updates_via_text(..., encode_segments_separately=True)` exists for exactly this situation and is used by MiniCPM-V. The override here mirrors that implementation. The alternative of normalising the prompt text (inserting `\\n` before an adjacent `<video>`) would change the prompt the model sees and only covers the leading boundary, so it was not taken.\n\nThe chat template shipped with the current public checkpoints inserts a newline between a text part and a following video part, so the OpenAI chat endpoint usually avoids this today; raw prompts, user-supplied placeholders in text, and older or custom templates still hit it.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63834?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795642051&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63834&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63834&signature=3215323e362eae5a22c57aa773ef1b3c6544bfe78dedf8b4292f278f64bbc46a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63834?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795642059&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63834&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63834&signature=fcf977ecead57fec77fcc0235534652b7d4fe938b5a9e891dd173dc93b6f4aae\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
